  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "update_ticket",
   "args": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6003",
    "status": "pending_approval",
    "note": "eng-deploy-tools is nested in release-operators (sensitive), which is nested in prod-admins (privileged), so its effective sensitivity is privileged. Manager approval APR-3102 (Sofia Andersson, decided 2026-10-26) is valid. Security approval APR-4001 requested from Hiroshi Tanabe (E1020) and is pending. No SoD conflicts. Not added yet."
   },
   "result": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6003",
    "status": "pending_approval"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Need to check nesting chain.\n\nI haven't added you to eng-deploy-tools yet. It still needs Security's approval, and I've sent that request.\n\n**Why Security has to approve:** eng-deploy-tools is set up inside release-operators, and release-operators is set up inside prod-admins. That means anyone in eng-deploy-tools also gets production admin access. Because of that, it needs approval from both your manager and Security.\n\n**Where the approvals stand:**\n- **Your manager:** Sofia Andersson approved it on Oct 26 (APR-3102). That approval counts, so she doesn't need to do anything else.\n- **Security:** I've asked Hiroshi Tanabe for approval (APR-4001). He hasn't responded yet.\n\nI also checked whether this access would clash with any groups you're already in. It doesn't.\n\nI've set ticket T-6003 to \"waiting for approval.\" Once Security approves, the desk can add you. If you only need the deploy dashboard and pipeline triggers, not production admin access, ask the group owner, Marco Bianchi. He may be able to change how the group is set up."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, it's nested inside prod-admins? I thought eng-deploy-tools was just the standard deploy group. Why does Security need to sign off on that? Sofia already approved it, so I'm not sure what else is needed."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, eng-deploy-tools is labeled \"standard\" by itself. The issue is how it's set up:\n\n- **eng-deploy-tools** (standard) is a member of\n- **release-operators** (sensitive), which is a member of\n- **prod-admins** (privileged: admin access to production infrastructure)\n\nBecause of that chain, anyone added to eng-deploy-tools also becomes a member of release-operators and prod-admins. We go by the highest level in the chain, and here that's privileged. Privileged access always needs approval from your manager and Security.\n\n**What's still needed:** Sofia's approval is all set, so she doesn't need to do anything more. The only thing left is Security's approval, which I've requested from Hiroshi Tanabe (APR-4001). Once he approves it, the desk can add you, and no one else needs to sign off.\n\n**If you only need the deploy dashboard and pipeline triggers:** you probably weren't expecting production admin access. Marco Bianchi owns eng-deploy-tools and release-operators. You could ask him whether eng-deploy-tools really needs to sit inside release-operators. If he takes it out of that chain, it would only need Sofia's approval, which you already have.\n\nYour ticket (T-6003) stays open as \"waiting for approval\" for now."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so the nesting is the problem, not the group itself. I didn't know eng-deploy-tools sat inside prod-admins through release-operators. I only need the deploy dashboard and pipeline triggers, not production admin, so asking Marco to take it out of that chain makes sense to me.\n\nCan you tell me when Hiroshi is likely to respond? And if Marco does change the setup, does that get rid of the Security approval requirement, or do I have to start over?"
  },
  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "check_approval_status",
   "args": {
    "approval_id": "APR-4001"
   },
   "result": {
    "approval_id": "APR-4001",
    "type": "access",
    "subject_employee_id": "E2301",
    "resource": "eng-deploy-tools",
    "approver_id": "E1020",
    "status": "pending",
    "requested_at": "2026-10-28T10:00:00-07:00",
    "decided_at": null,
    "created_in_run": true,
    "log_index": 9,
    "approver_name": "Hiroshi Tanabe"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I just checked again, and Hiroshi still hasn't responded. I can't tell you when he will. He's active, not on leave, so the request is waiting with him and doesn't need to go to anyone else.\n\n**If Marco changes the setup, you don't have to start over:**\n\n- **If he takes eng-deploy-tools out of release-operators:** the group stops being privileged and goes back to standard. Then only Sofia's approval is needed, which you already have.\n- **Sofia's approval has a time limit:** it counts for 14 days from when she approved it on Oct 26, so until about **Nov 9**. After that, she'd have to approve again.\n- **If Marco makes a different change:** say he keeps eng-deploy-tools inside release-operators and only takes release-operators out of prod-admins. Then the group would be \"sensitive.\" That needs approval from Sofia and the group owner, which is Marco himself. So it's simplest if he takes eng-deploy-tools out of release-operators.\n- **What happens next:** once Marco has made the change, message the desk on ticket T-6003. We'll check the setup again, and if the only thing left is Sofia's approval, we'll add you right away. The Security request will just no longer be needed.\n\nIf Hiroshi approves before Marco makes any change, we can add you then. But you'd get production admin access too, so if you don't want that, it's better to wait for Marco.\n\nYour ticket (T-6003) stays open as \"waiting for approval\" for now."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Got it, thanks. I'll ask Marco to take eng-deploy-tools out of release-operators, and I'll update T-6003 once he's done it. Sofia's approval is still good until Nov 9, so I should be fine if he gets to it before then."
  },
  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "update_ticket",
   "args": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6003",
    "status": "pending_approval",
    "note": "Employee only needs the deploy dashboard and pipeline triggers, not prod admin. Employee will ask group owner Marco Bianchi (E2303) to take eng-deploy-tools out of release-operators. If that's done, the group becomes standard and manager approval APR-3102 is enough (counts until ~2026-11-09). Re-check nesting before adding. Security approval APR-4001 is still pending with E1020."
   },
   "result": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6003",
    "status": "pending_approval"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "That's right. If Marco takes eng-deploy-tools out of release-operators before Nov 9, Sofia's approval is enough on its own, and we can add you once you let us know.\n\nI've added a note to T-6003 about the plan, and it stays open as \"waiting for approval.\" When you come back after Marco's change, we'll check the group setup again before adding you. If something else changes in the meantime, we'll tell you what that means for your request.\n\nThanks, Dev!"
  }
